---
title: Fewer non-IT postings cluttering search
date: 2026-08-07
summary: Postings our category dictionaries could never place — painters, drivers, warehouse stockers pulled in by broad company career-page crawls — no longer show up in search or filters.
type: changelog
tags:
  - job-seekers
  - catalogue
draft: false
---

A lot of our sources are a company's whole career page, not just its engineering roles —
so a crawl brings back everything that page lists, IT or not. Most of that gets caught and
kept out on the way in. Some of it wasn't: titles generic enough that nothing recognized
them as tech *or* as clearly not tech, so they sat in the catalogue with no
[specialization](/jobs) at all — unsearchable by role, unfilterable, just noise between
the postings you were actually looking for.

That noise is now out of search and out of every category filter. Nothing was deleted —
every posting is still stored exactly as it was, and if a title later gets a real category,
it reappears in search on its own, no action needed on our end. We checked all 36
specializations (backend, frontend, design, management, sales, and the rest) before and
after: every one of them is unchanged. Only the "couldn't tell what this even is" bucket
is gone.
